# Compiled test binaries are ignored; their SOURCES never are. The
# negation is written against the same prefix as the exclusion, because a
# general "!**/*.nim" is easy to defeat and once cost this repository its
# whole test suite in commit 891f9a8.
tests/**/test_*
!tests/**/test_*.nim
!tests/**/*.nim
tests/data/
.geist-koerper/
koerper/
*.bfx1
*.bfx2
*.geistdb
*.config.json
.env
.env.*

nimble.develop
nimble.paths
nimbledeps
.iron/conventions/
tests/.otter/results/

# legacy implementation kept for reference during rearchitecture
.geist-legacy/
*.ge1st
*.keys
*.ledger
*.b1
*.b2
*.b3
.geist-sidecar/

# Compiled example binaries, same rule as the tests above: the sources are
# tracked, the products of `nimble examples` are not.
examples/geist_*
!examples/geist_*.nim
# The write lease. It names a live process, so it is meaningless in a repo.
.geist-lock

# The user's own settings: paths, pins and endpoints for THIS machine.
# The template beside it is tracked; what someone fills in is not.
userconfig.toml
